# Line endings are pinned here because nothing else pins them: core.autocrlf
# is false on the machines this repo is developed on, so whatever a tool
# happens to write is what gets committed. On 18 August 2026 something
# rewrote 11 files from LF to CRLF in a working tree, turning 14 real changed
# lines into ~1,799 phantom ones and hiding an edit to test_security_guard.py
# inside a whitespace diff. The cause was never identified, which is the
# argument for pinning rather than for finding it.
#
# Everything here is text: Markdown, JSON, Python, HTML/JSX/CSS/SVG. None of
# it needs CRLF, and every tool that reads it accepts LF on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

# If a Windows shell script is ever added, it needs CRLF to run.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
